            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0526" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/686: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-10-03T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 3,
                                1927—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 3—7:13
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to Department’s October 1, 6 p.m., I am preparing to undertake to carry
                    out recommendations contained in paragraph 2 [<hi rendition="#italic">7</hi>] of
                    my September 26, 4 p.m. and am so informing American warehousemen as well as
                    importers in American ships. Full report by mail. Repeated to the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
